member.remarks:
Lifecycle per connection:

// Acquire
PooledReceiveContext ctx = ObjectPoolManager.Get<PooledReceiveContext>();
ctx.EnsureArgsBound();

// Use (many times — SAEA is reused for every packet on this connection)
int n = await ctx.ReceiveAsync(socket, buffer, offset, count);

// Release on Dispose
ctx.ResetForPool();
ObjectPoolManager.Return<PooledReceiveContext>(ctx);




Bug fixes vs previous revision:



    Static AsyncReceiveCompleted now resolves the result directly on a reusable
     stored on the owning
    , removing the per-receive
     allocation.



     is no longer async: it returns
     directly, preserving the
    synchronous fast-path and AggressiveInlining.

example.code:
var timer = new TimingWheel();
timer.Activate();
timer.Register(connection);
// ...
timer.Deactivate();

remarks.para:
The cancellationToken parameter is intentionally unused beyond the initial
 check;
the actual token is forwarded to BeginAcceptAsync internally.
